libdatachannel 0.24.6's PeerConnection::initSctpTransport() checks for an SCTP transport and
creates one without a lock, unlike initDtlsTransport(). When ICE connects before the remote
description is committed (the offerer, whose ICE transport starts on the answer before
processRemoteDescription() stores it), processRemoteDescription() starts the DTLS transport and
then the SCTP transport once DTLS is connected, while the DTLS transport's Connected callback
starts it too, on another thread: both create one, the second replaces the first, and the first,
destroyed, stops the DTLS transport under it ("SCTP early shutdown", "DTLS closed"), so the
connection goes to failed. webcpp::webrtc's native tests met it about once in 3000 runs under
load (2026-11-23). This patch gives initSctpTransport() a mutex of its own, as
initDtlsTransport() has. Remove this file once the libdatachannel that
tools/libdatachannel/pin.json pins serializes initSctpTransport(): build.py then fails, saying so.

This patch changes files of libdatachannel, which the Mozilla Public License 2.0 covers, and is
itself under that licence.

diff --git a/src/impl/peerconnection.hpp b/src/impl/peerconnection.hpp
--- a/src/impl/peerconnection.hpp
+++ b/src/impl/peerconnection.hpp
@@ -154,6 +154,7 @@ private:
 	shared_ptr<IceTransport> mIceTransport;
 	shared_ptr<DtlsTransport> mDtlsTransport;
 	std::mutex mDtlsTransportInitMutex;
+	std::mutex mSctpTransportInitMutex;
 	shared_ptr<SctpTransport> mSctpTransport;
 
 	std::unordered_map<uint16_t, weak_ptr<DataChannel>> mDataChannels; // by stream ID
diff --git a/src/impl/peerconnection.cpp b/src/impl/peerconnection.cpp
--- a/src/impl/peerconnection.cpp
+++ b/src/impl/peerconnection.cpp
@@ -304,6 +304,10 @@ shared_ptr<DtlsTransport> PeerConnection::initDtlsTransport() {
 
 shared_ptr<SctpTransport> PeerConnection::initSctpTransport() {
 	try {
+		// The DTLS transport's Connected callback and processRemoteDescription() may both start
+		// the SCTP transport: the second must find the first's rather than replace it, which
+		// would destroy the first and stop the DTLS transport under it.
+		std::lock_guard lock(mSctpTransportInitMutex);
 		if (auto transport = std::atomic_load(&mSctpTransport))
 			return transport;
 
